 "Header": {
  "BPX": "1.0.0",
  "Title": "BYD FC4680 LFP/graphite 4680 cylindrical cell",
  "Description": "Parameter set for the BYD FC4680, an LFP/graphite 4680 cylindrical cell. Geometry and the phase inventory are identified in this work from the teardown of Liu et al. (2025, doi:10.1149/1945-7111/ae1e33) and from an over-determined system of mass, capacity and volume closures, which determines the cathode porosity, the can wall and the separator thickness that no source reports. The ELECTROCHEMISTRY is transferred from About:Energy's BPX parameterisation of an LFP/graphite 2 Ah 18650 (github.com/About-Energy-OpenSource/About-Energy-BPX-Parameterisation), used under CC-BY-SA 4.0; electrolyte transport is Nyman et al. (2008). KNOWN LIMITATION: LiFePO4 discharges through a two-phase transformation, so the solid diffusivity here is an EFFECTIVE quantity absorbing phase-boundary kinetics into a Fickian form, and the model cannot represent voltage hysteresis. Do not read the diffusivity as a material property. CALIBRATED (paper 1 v2, Section 5.2, 1 Oct 2026) on the author's bench test of cell c1 (1C and 2C discharges to 2.0 V at 25 C, three surface thermocouples; data released with this set): cathode D_s x0.767 (r_s^2/D_s = 4740 s), E_a,Ds = 18.8 kJ/mol, anode theta0 = 0.796, and an end-of-lithiation drop added to the About:Energy cathode potential, -1.4 V ((theta - 1 + w)/w)^n for theta > 1 - w, w = 0.131, n = 2.58, which the window-guarded fit lacked; the OCP table of the positive electrode therefore runs to theta = 1. The heat-transfer coefficient is the measured 22.4 W/m^2/K of the bench fixture (hA = 0.337 W/K). The calibration also identified a clamp contact heat of 1.34 mOhm outside the voltage path; it is a property of the clamp and is NOT in this file. VERSION 1.2 (1 Oct 2026): the calibrated values above. VERSION 1.1 (27 Sep 2026): corrected the version 1.0 files, which carried the solid conductivity sigma instead of the effective eps_s*sigma the solver uses and a zero heat-transfer coefficient. LICENCE: CC-BY-SA 4.0, because it incorporates About:Energy material. The rest of this dataset is CC BY 4.0.",
  "References": "Liu et al. 2025; About:Energy LFP BPX parameterisation (CC-BY-SA 4.0); Nyman et al. 2008.",
  "Model": "DFN"
 },
